# HexPal Testing Rules

**hexpal-project.mdc** requires: every Utilities/ file has a *Tests.swift; tests use known reference values; run full suite after any change.

## Test Structure
- Every test file maps 1:1 to a source file (ColorConverter.swift → ColorConverterTests.swift)
- Import only XCTest and the module under test. No AppKit/SwiftUI in utility tests.
- Use XCTAssertEqual with accuracy parameter for all floating point (accuracy: 0.001 unless noted)
- Group related tests with // MARK: - SectionName

## Test Naming
- Pattern: test_functionName_inputDescription_expectedOutput()
- Examples:
  - test_hexString_pureRed_returnsFF0000()
  - test_wcagContrast_blackOnWhite_returns21()
  - test_apcaContrast_swappedColors_returnsDifferentValue()

## Test Data
Use well-known reference values:
- WCAG: Black on White = 21:1, White on White = 1:1
- APCA: Validate against myndex.com/APCA calculator
- OKLCH: Validate against oklch.org converter
- Hex: Pure red = #FF0000 = rgb(255, 0, 0)
- Include edge cases: pure black, pure white, mid-gray, boundary thresholds (exactly 4.5:1)

## Regression Prevention
- Write the test file FIRST before implementing the feature
- After ANY code change, run the full test suite
- If a test fails, fix it BEFORE continuing
- Never delete a passing test to make a build succeed

## Performance Tests
- XCTMeasure for computations that must complete < 100ms
- Color conversion: 1000 iterations < 50ms total
- Contrast calculation: 1000 iterations < 20ms total
